#
# Reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# One vulnerability, misconfiguration, or secret rule ID per line.
# A line starting with # is a comment and suppresses nothing. Remove the
# leading # to activate an example:
#
#   CVE-2019-14697 exp:2027-01-01
#   AVD-DS-0002
#   generic-unwanted-rule
#
# `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` limits a suppression to that date. After it, trivy
# reports the finding again.
#
# This file sits beside the configured trivy.yml, so the scan uses it.
# A .trivyignore at the repository root applies only when this file is
# absent; the two are never merged.

# DS-0002 "Specify at least 1 USER command ... with non-root user":
# Every Dockerfile in this repo produces a GitHub Actions job-container image
# (see .github/workflows/build_*.yml `container:`). A non-root USER cannot
# write GITHUB_WORKSPACE, which is host-mounted and owned by the runner uid;
# that breaks actions/checkout and every subsequent build step. These images
# must run as root, so the finding does not apply here.
#
# DS-0029 on the rocm meta-package install is suppressed inline at its single
# occurrence in Dockerfiles/hip-libraries-cuda-ubuntu.Dockerfile, so it is
# intentionally not listed here (a bare ID would suppress it repo-wide).
AVD-DS-0002
